<title>USA: Western Resources antitrust period expires.</title>
<headline>Western Resources antitrust period expires.</headline>
<dateline>TOPEKA, Kan 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Resources Inc said the 30-day waiting period on its hostile $3.5 billion bid for ADT Ltd has expired without action from federal antitrust authorities.</p>
<p>The company, which owns 27.1 percent of ADT, said the move will allow it to proceed with its planned acquisition.</p>
<p>ADT has rejected Western Resources' bid of 22-1/2 per share.</p>
<p>Shares of ADT were unchanged at 22-3/4.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1700))</p>
